From: tyn-patches <tyn-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:18:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: use highp float in GLES fragment shaders when supported
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

可向上游提交。

Previously ShaderHeaderFrag hardcoded `precision mediump float;` on all GL_ES
targets. On strict FP16 fragment drivers, sampling large texture atlases such
as 3072x6000 FONT.PNG introduces up to ~3 px UV quantization error, clipping
glyph edges and bleeding adjacent cells.

Prefer `precision highp float;` when GL_FRAGMENT_PRECISION_HIGH is defined,
falling back to `precision mediump float;` otherwise. Audited all shaders
under src/shaders/opengl/*_{vert,frag}.glsl: only the Renderable3D_* pairs
share uniforms between vertex and fragment stages, and all shared uniforms
already use UNIFORM_PRECISION, so keeping UNIFORM_PRECISION as mediump in
ShaderHeaderES introduces no precision mismatch.

Verified on MuMu emulator (Android 15, not a real device) with steins;gate
(sg-pc, Steam + 2018 CN patch).

diff --git a/src/renderer/opengl/shader.cpp b/src/renderer/opengl/shader.cpp
index 91a0460b720b229509aa61b180716bb1e45865e8..7795af10ea08b1bae7ab6f8a4a357c3b6ac2613a 100644
--- a/src/renderer/opengl/shader.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer/opengl/shader.cpp
@@ -30,8 +30,8 @@ static char const ShaderHeaderVert[] =
     "#define VERTEX_SHADER\n#ifdef GL_ES\nprecision highp float;\n#endif\n\n";
 static GLint const ShaderHeaderVertLength = sizeof(ShaderHeaderVert) - 1;
 static char const ShaderHeaderFrag[] =
-    "#define FRAGMENT_SHADER\n#ifdef GL_ES\nprecision mediump "
-    "float;\n#endif\n\n";
+    "#define FRAGMENT_SHADER\n#ifdef GL_ES\n#ifdef GL_FRAGMENT_PRECISION_HIGH\n"
+    "precision highp float;\n#else\nprecision mediump float;\n#endif\n#endif\n\n";
 static GLint const ShaderHeaderFragLength = sizeof(ShaderHeaderFrag) - 1;
 
 int ShaderCompiler::PrintParameter(char* dest, int destSz, char const* name,
